    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_19970403.0524\n\nLONDON, April 3 , 1997 (AFP)\n\nClimber killed abseiling on Britain's highest peak\n\n\n\n\nA climber who fell while abseiling on Britain's highest mountain has died from his injuries, police said Thursday.\n\nThe man was climbing with a friend on Observation Gully near the summit of 4,406-foot (1,300-meter) Ben Nevis in Scotland when he fell. The second man also suffered \"serious injuries.\"\n\nThe pair were airlifted to hospital in Fort William where the first climber died from his injuries, a police spokesman said.\n\nNeither climber was named by police.",
